le">6</text><title>1903: British forces take Kano in February and occupy Sokoto in March</title></g><g class="rf-ev"><line x1="740.0" x2="740.0" y1="160" y2="166"/><circle cx="740.0" cy="160" r="8"/><text x="740.0" y="164" text-anchor="middle">7</text><title>1903: Sultan Attahiru I is killed fighting the British at Burmi in July</title></g><text class="rf-axis" x="20" y="200">1804 CE</text><text class="rf-axis" x="740" y="200" text-anchor="end">1903 CE</text></svg><figcaption>Relative power on the Institute's 0–10 scale (each profile scaled to its own peak). Numbers mark the key events below.</figcaption></figure><ol class="rf-events"><li><span class="rf-year">1804</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/usman-dan-fodio">Usman dan Fodio</a> makes his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hijra">hijra</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gudu">Gudu</a> and declares <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jihad">jihad</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hausa">Hausa</a> kings</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1808</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jihad">Jihad</a> forces storm <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alkalawa">Alkalawa</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gobir">Gobir</a> capital, killing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yunfa">Sultan Yunfa</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1817</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/usman-dan-fodio">Dan Fodio</a> dies; his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-bello">Muhammad Bello</a> becomes <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan-of-sokoto">Sultan of Sokoto</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1886</span><span class="rf-text">Britain charters the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/royal-niger-company">Royal Niger Company</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1900</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-lugard">Frederick Lugard</a> proclaims the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northern-nigeria-protectorate">Protectorate of Northern Nigeria</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1903</span><span class="rf-text">British forces take <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kano">Kano</a> in February and occupy Sokoto in March</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1903</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> Attahiru I is killed fighting the British at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burmi">Burmi</a> in July</span></li></ol>
